<Concept title="Reyburn combat delivery" section="States">
<p>Implementation contract for #563 and #714, extending /states/bosses. This is
remake reliability work: original attack-selection probabilities, damage-budget
phase transitions and event-frame mapping remain unresolved.</p>
<ul>
<li>The model, charge, melee arc and knockback MUST share local +Z facing.
Turning MUST respect the authored degrees-per-second limit. Attack facing MUST
lock when the final striking clip starts.</li>
<li>Selection MUST respect inclusive minimum/maximum range and ignore zero or
negative weights. A retreat beyond impact reach MUST avoid melee damage.</li>
<li>Every chain clip preceding the strike MUST play for its resolved duration
without damage. Loop preludes MUST run the authored lp_loops count, default one.
Missing clips MUST use a bounded 0.35 second prelude / 0.8 second strike fallback.
The final clip MUST release once at windup_frac (default 0.55) of its duration.
The existing projectile volley releases together at that point; staggered
original breath events remain a separate fidelity task.</li>
<li>Walking MUST advance its animation rather than restart each physics tick.
Enrage MUST NOT replace an in-progress attack clip. Its speed/cooldown modifiers
remain existing remake tuning, as do the 35% enrage and 50% flight gates.</li>
</ul>
<p>Validation: reyburn_combat_tests.gd seeds geometry and timeline boundaries;
reyburn_combat_probe.tscn repeats them with the real z_001 rig in s01z_na1.</p>
</Concept>
